    <Ab_initio>Gaussian B3LYP/6-31G*</Ab_initio>
    <Fit_systems>SH_2</Fit_systems>
  </E_rep>
  <Misc>
    <Accuracy>For a test set of 28 molecules containing the elements S,O,N,C,H the RMS 
              error in bondlengths was 0.033 ang. and 3.1 deg. in bond angles. Frequencies 
              for 8 molecules showed a RMS error of 5.4 % wrt experiment. All files in this
              sulfur set show a consistent overbinding of roughly 10
              kcal/mole.
    </Accuracy>
    <Publications>
      <Fit>Niehaus T.A., Elstner M., Frauenheim T., Suhai S.;
           J. Mol. Struct.-THEOCHEM;541; pp. 185 (2001)
      </Fit>
      <Other id="1" >Daminelli G., Widany J., Di Carlo A., Lugli P.;
                     J. Chem. Phys.; 115; pp. 4919 (2001) 
      </Other>
      <Other id="2" >Fabian J., Diaz L.A., Seifert G., Niehaus T.A.;
                     J. Mol. Struct.-THEOCHEM; 594; pp. 41 (2002)
      </Other>
      <Other id="3" >Joswig J.O., Seifert G., Niehaus T.A., Springborg M.;
                     J. Phys. Chem. B; 107; pp. 2897 (2003)
      </Other>
    </Publications>
    <Notes>Sulfur set was fitted to perform calculations on bio-molecules.
           The d-Orbitals were included because S-C bonds came out far
	   too long and the SO_2 bond angle was completely wrong.The 
	   actual compression radius of the d-Orbitals had a minor influence
	   on the results. 
    </Notes>
  </Misc>
</Documentation>


